WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.833
- I just moved here.

00:00:00.833 --> 00:00:02.820
So you first moved here a while back,

00:00:02.820 --> 00:00:03.653
but what was it like

00:00:03.653 --> 00:00:05.790
when you first-
- 1976 I moved here.

00:00:05.790 --> 00:00:07.290
- Did you love it?
- I loved it.

00:00:07.290 --> 00:00:08.123
Yeah.
- me too.

00:00:08.123 --> 00:00:09.450
- I grew up in Philly

00:00:09.450 --> 00:00:11.109
and I'd been-
- That's not far.

00:00:11.109 --> 00:00:12.570
Yeah, yeah.
- It's not far. It's not far.

00:00:12.570 --> 00:00:15.270
I've been here a few times
because my sister lived here,

00:00:15.270 --> 00:00:18.144
my sister lived on, on West End Avenue,

00:00:18.144 --> 00:00:20.580
so she was very nice to
let me sleep on her couch

00:00:20.580 --> 00:00:24.600
for probably, I don't know,
four months until I got my feet.

00:00:24.600 --> 00:00:25.720
- That's nice.
- On the ground yeah.

00:00:25.720 --> 00:00:27.840
- Yeah. 'Cause it's not a cheap city.

00:00:27.840 --> 00:00:29.100
No. It's yeah...
- No, no.

00:00:29.100 --> 00:00:31.893
Although I can tell you that in 1976,

00:00:32.760 --> 00:00:37.760
my budget for my apartment
was $150 a month.

00:00:37.770 --> 00:00:39.990
- So you lived in a closet?
- Right.

00:00:39.990 --> 00:00:41.700
Well...
- Of someone else's.

00:00:41.700 --> 00:00:43.710
- Of someone else's closet right.

00:00:43.710 --> 00:00:45.360
Well, that what, what happened was it was,

00:00:45.360 --> 00:00:47.040
I, I had figured that it
was a hundred and fifty,

00:00:47.040 --> 00:00:48.630
I don't know where I got the math on that,

00:00:48.630 --> 00:00:51.300
but that's what I, that's how
I, that's what I had decided.

00:00:51.300 --> 00:00:54.000
- Yeah.
- And so I went into this,

00:00:54.000 --> 00:00:55.830
I saw an ad in the back
of "The Village Voice",

00:00:55.830 --> 00:01:00.660
and it said, "Artists,
actors, musicians, residents".

00:01:00.660 --> 00:01:02.910
And I thought, well,
that's, that sounds good.

00:01:02.910 --> 00:01:05.296
It was basically a flop
house. Really, I mean...

00:01:05.296 --> 00:01:06.827
(audience laughs)
(Kelly chuckles)

00:01:06.827 --> 00:01:08.040
I don't, I guess there were some,

00:01:08.040 --> 00:01:10.380
some artists there, but not a lot.

00:01:10.380 --> 00:01:12.060
- Like, do you mind living with rats?

00:01:12.060 --> 00:01:12.903
- Exactly yeah.
- Yeah.

00:01:12.903 --> 00:01:14.280
- Yeah exactly.
- Yeah.

00:01:14.280 --> 00:01:16.620
- But I walked into the,
into the rental office

00:01:16.620 --> 00:01:19.320
and the guy said, "No, we
don't have any single room

00:01:19.320 --> 00:01:23.610
apartments, but we do have
a two room apartment".

00:01:23.610 --> 00:01:26.700
So basically it was a
kitchen and another room.

00:01:26.700 --> 00:01:30.540
And I said, he said, "That's
three and a quarter a month".

00:01:30.540 --> 00:01:31.650
And I said, "I can't afford that

00:01:31.650 --> 00:01:32.820
and I don't have a roommate".

00:01:32.820 --> 00:01:34.440
And he said, "What about this guy?"

00:01:34.440 --> 00:01:35.765
I'm sitting on the couch and I, I looked,

00:01:35.765 --> 00:01:37.567
"I don't know this guys" and he goes,

00:01:37.567 --> 00:01:38.565
"You wanna live together?"

00:01:38.565 --> 00:01:39.750
And I was like, "Yeah, okay.

00:01:39.750 --> 00:01:41.670
Yeah, okay, we'll live together".

00:01:41.670 --> 00:01:44.254
Yeah. And we lived
together for four years.

00:01:44.254 --> 00:01:45.930
- Oh my gosh!
- Yeah. In fact,

00:01:45.930 --> 00:01:47.943
I just had lunch with him the other day.

00:01:50.105 --> 00:01:51.120
- What?
- He was a,

00:01:51.120 --> 00:01:52.803
he was a classical pianist.

00:01:53.699 --> 00:01:54.593
- Well you were both musicians,

00:01:54.593 --> 00:01:55.820
so yeah that's cool.
- Yeah.

00:01:55.820 --> 00:01:58.890
He was, he's great, great.

00:01:58.890 --> 00:02:01.170
Played beautiful, I
mean, I'd be, you know,

00:02:01.170 --> 00:02:02.160
in the middle of the afternoon,

00:02:02.160 --> 00:02:04.050
he worked nights at the Copacabana,

00:02:04.050 --> 00:02:05.100
and in the middle

00:02:05.100 --> 00:02:06.270
of the after-
- This is a TV show.

00:02:06.270 --> 00:02:08.860
This is like, yeah what?
(Kelly clasps hands)

00:02:08.860 --> 00:02:10.170
- Yeah, yeah.

00:02:10.170 --> 00:02:13.080
I'd, he'd come home and he'd be playing,

00:02:13.080 --> 00:02:14.280
you know, Chopin or whatever,

00:02:14.280 --> 00:02:16.350
and it was, it was, it was really cool.

00:02:16.350 --> 00:02:17.183
- That's incred...

00:02:17.183 --> 00:02:18.180
I actually moved out to LA

00:02:18.180 --> 00:02:20.100
with some random person I did not know.

00:02:20.100 --> 00:02:20.933
- Really?
- Yeah.

00:02:20.933 --> 00:02:22.599
She just needed a roommate.
I was like, "I'll do it".

00:02:22.599 --> 00:02:26.213
I was like, and I moved from
Texas to LA with a stranger.

00:02:26.213 --> 00:02:27.046
- Wow.
- Yeah.

00:02:27.046 --> 00:02:29.070
- And how long did that last?
- Not long.

00:02:29.070 --> 00:02:30.792
We moved into a place and it burned down,

00:02:30.792 --> 00:02:31.968
so yeah.
- Uh huh.

00:02:31.968 --> 00:02:33.810
- Then I slept in my car for a few days

00:02:33.810 --> 00:02:35.400
and then tried out for a
show called "American Idol",

00:02:35.400 --> 00:02:37.795
so it all worked out.
(audience cheers)

00:02:37.795 --> 00:02:38.628
It all worked out. Yeah.

00:02:38.628 --> 00:02:39.816
- What a story.

00:02:39.816 --> 00:02:41.107
I mean that's quite a story.
- Life.

00:02:41.107 --> 00:02:41.940
Yeah.
- What a story.

00:02:41.940 --> 00:02:43.320
- I feel like everyone in this industry

00:02:43.320 --> 00:02:46.080
has some crazy thing where
you've either lived in your car

00:02:46.080 --> 00:02:48.150
or on a mattress in
someone's house, or yeah,

00:02:48.150 --> 00:02:50.970
It's like, yeah, you really
gotta want your dream.

00:02:50.970 --> 00:02:51.803
- You do.
- Yeah.

00:02:51.803 --> 00:02:52.636
You gotta have

00:02:52.636 --> 00:02:53.469
the hunger as well.
- The universe makes you

00:02:53.469 --> 00:02:54.843
really want it.

